<resources>

    <!--
        Every user-facing string in the app.

        Notes for translators:
        · Amounts and chip counts are formatted by the app and arrive as placeholders. Never
          translate the digits, and keep the placeholder in a position that reads naturally.
        · "Chips" always means the physical tokens on the table. "Cash" always means real money.
          The distinction is the app's central hazard and must survive translation.
        · A "big blind" (BB) and a "small blind" are poker terms; most languages keep them.
        · Positional placeholders (%1$s) are used everywhere so word order can change freely.
    -->

